  message: "Partly addressed on the PR 3 branch (stable-id v16, jgstern-agent/feat/stable-id-v16, commit 315063612, WI-bubak): a Swift declaration's OWN generic clause and where-constraints are now hashed, with type parameters renamed by position; the 3 TCA bound-only tie groups split. STILL OPEN: (1) an enclosing extension's where-clause is not hashed. Repro: extension Array where Element: P { func f() {} } next to the same extension with Element: Q gives both Array.f the same stable id (split only by occurrence order). Hashing an enclosing extension's constraints into its members was outside the WI-bubak ruling (own clause only); owner call. (2) argument labels and (3) static-vs-instance are untouched."  # d004
